From a0e89d4733ad911d543092edf2f4b84d830c22cd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt Liberty <mliberty@precisioninno.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 03:26:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] python: share the per-tool wrapper library settings in
 a macro

Every tool's py_wrap repeated the same defines, visibility, alwayslink and
common deps. python_wrap_library in bazel/python_wrap_cc.bzl holds them,
so each tool lists only what is its own.

modules_test's /proc/self/maps check is Linux-only, so it is now a separate
test skipped elsewhere; the check that every module loads from the one
library still runs everywhere.

Signed-off-by: Matt Liberty <mliberty@precisioninno.com>
